{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "text": {
        "type": "plain_text",
        "text": "🛑 Decision needed: release/1.0.0 → main",
        "emoji": true
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "text": {
        "type": "mrkdwn",
        "text": "The merge conflicts, so *nothing was created*. main mirrors production and holds changes release/1.0.0 never received. *Do not resolve this or merge main into release/1.0.0*: that would deploy it without a new release candidate."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rich_text",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "rich_text_section",
          "elements": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Conflicted files",
              "style": {
                "bold": true
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "rich_text_list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "indent": 0,
          "elements": [
            {
              "type": "rich_text_section",
              "elements": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "app/models/seat.rb",
                  "style": {
                    "code": true
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "rich_text_section",
              "elements": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "config/settings.yml",
                  "style": {
                    "code": true
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "text": {
        "type": "mrkdwn",
        "text": "*Option 1: take main's changes into a new candidate* (usually right)\nRun create_release_candidate with releaseType patch, merge origin/main into the new release branch, promote it with release_version, have Ops deploy it to every production host, then downmerge that release into main, which is clean by then."
      },
      "accessory": {
        "type": "button",
        "action_id": "start_request",
        "text": {
          "type": "plain_text",
          "text": "Plan a patch RC",
          "emoji": true
        },
        "style": "primary",
        "value": "{\"q\":\"create an RC patch\"}",
        "confirm": {
          "title": {
            "type": "plain_text",
            "text": "Create a release candidate?"
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "plain_text",
            "text": "Plans \"create an RC patch\". If the plan has no warnings it applies at once, without an Approve step: a release branch, tag and pull request on origin."
          },
          "confirm": {
            "type": "plain_text",
            "text": "Create it"
          },
          "deny": {
            "type": "plain_text",
            "text": "Back"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "text": {
        "type": "mrkdwn",
        "text": "*Option 2: leave them out of release/1.0.0*\ncut release-1.0.0-into-main-&lt;unix-timestamp&gt; off origin/main, merge origin/release/1.0.0 into it, resolve app/models/seat.rb, config/settings.yml, and open a pull request into main titled \"Release 1.0.0 to main\". Say in it that main will then differ from what production runs."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "block_id": "footer",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "mrkdwn",
          "text": "<https://github.com/officespacesoftware/versioner/blob/master/docs/manual-downmerge.md|Manual downmerge procedure> · requested by <@U0REQ> · <https://cursor.com/agents/bc-7f3a|agent>"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
